{#
   Args for checkpoints.canvas.md.xml.jinja — the twelve graded checkpoints.

   Rules:
     - No date literals. Due_Date and Due_Day come from global_args, and the
       day keys are the *session* keys (CP1 is due at Session 6, so it reads
       S06_DAY). Move a session date and the checkpoint follows it.
     - Due_Time follows what is being handed in, and must match the handout's
       Submission line. Work students carry to class (CP1-CP4, CP9) is
       CLASS_START_TIME; repo state (CP5-CP8, CP11) is END_OF_DAY, because the
       deadline is "merged," not "brought"; live work (CP4, CP10, CP12) says so
       in Due_Note.
     - Points is always 100 — the rubric grid is out of 100. Weight is carried
       by the assignment group, not by points. Weight here is prose for the
       student, and must agree with the syllabus table and course_content.
     - Write `&amp;` for an ampersand: Title lands in an XML attribute.
     - Ids are permanent. Renaming one orphans the Canvas assignment.
#}
